start     book
terminals word

# A book somebody put away as unfit, kept in the D'ni city's quarantine chamber (design §4.2). The one
# found book allowed to argue with itself: BookCheck fails any book here that comes out coherent. Each
# alternative should be a mistake a reader can see in the world and learn to recognise in their own.
#
# Two mistakes a book, so it comes out wounded and in the grip of phenomena but nowhere near collapse:
# BookCheck holds every one between the phenomena's floor and collapse's threshold.

book = [torn_climate] | [flooded_desert] | [warring_sizes] | [settled_ruins]

torn_climate = age [cold_stone] landmass frozen scorching tropical climate

flooded_desert = age arid landmass flooded rock [wet_sky]

warring_sizes = age colossal minuscule landmass [wild_weather]

settled_ruins = age villagers ruins structures trees arid landmass

cold_stone = packed_ice | snow_block

wet_sky = drenched weather | verdant climate

wild_weather = blizzard inferno weather | parched deluge weather
